From: ArchPad Project <https://github.com/pipa-mainline>
Subject: [PATCH] iio-sensor-proxy: start polling for pre-existing clients on discovery

If a D-Bus client calls ClaimAccelerometer() or another claim method
before name_acquired_handler finishes driver initialization, the client
is inserted into data->clients, but driver_set_polling is not invoked.

Mirror the logic in sensor_changes: if clients already claimed the sensor
type, mark sensor_startup_dbus_event_delayed and call driver_set_polling.
---
--- a/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
+++ b/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
@@ -780,6 +780,11 @@ name_acquired_handler (GDBusConnection *connection,
 		}

 		DEVICE_FOR_TYPE(i) = sensor_device;
+
+		if (g_hash_table_size (data->clients[i]) > 0) {
+			data->sensor_startup_dbus_event_delayed[i] = TRUE;
+			driver_set_polling (sensor_device, TRUE);
+		}
 	}

 	if (!any_sensors_left (data))
